<% content_for :title, "Break this text into claims" %>
<h1>Break this text into claims</h1>
<p class="lede">From <%= link_to @source.title, source_path(@source) %>. Galedra does not break a text into claims itself: it runs no model, and splitting sentences is not a breakdown. An assistant or a person does it, and every claim they record is signed and theirs.</p>
<% if @recorded.positive? %><p class="meta"><%= link_to pluralize(@recorded, "claim"), source_path(@source) %> recorded from this text so far.</p><% end %>
<% if @error %><div class="card errors"><p><%= @error %></p></div><% end %>

<h2>With your assistant</h2>
<p>If your assistant is connected to Galedra, copy this to it. It breaks the text into one claim per assertion, records them as a check filed under this text, gives each its own first reading, and hands you the link to share.</p>
<pre class="prompt" data-copy><%= @prompt %></pre>
<p class="meta">Not connected yet? <%= link_to "Connect an assistant", new_assistant_path %>. One that cannot connect can write a bundle for you to paste on <%= link_to "Record an investigation", new_investigation_path %>.</p>

<h2>Open to any volunteer</h2>
<% if @tasks.any? %>
  <p><%= pluralize(@tasks.size, "claim-extraction task") %> on this text, one per <%= Tasks::Types::EXCERPT_CAP.to_fs(:delimited) %>-character window, so a volunteer's assistant reads all of the text it is given:</p>
  <ul><% @tasks.each do |task| %><li><%= link_to "Task #{short_id(task.id)}", task_path(task) %> · <%= task.status.downcase %><% if task.cancelled_reason.present? %> (<%= task.cancelled_reason.downcase.tr("_", " ") %>)<% end %></li><% end %></ul>
  <p class="meta">Breaking the text down yourself, here or through your own assistant, closes the ones still open.</p>
<% else %>
  <p class="muted">No extraction task is open on this text.</p>
<% end %>

<h2>By hand</h2>
<p class="meta">One assertion per claim: split anything joined by "and", a list, or a "because". Keep what a text says (<code>TEXTUAL</code>) apart from whether it is true, and an opinion (<code>NORMATIVE</code>) apart from a fact. Check wording shows where a claim may hold more than one assertion, and records nothing.</p>
<%= form_with url: claims_source_path(@source), method: :post do |f| %>
  <% @rows.each_with_index do |row, i| %>
    <div class="proposal">
      <label>Claim <%= text_field_tag "claims[#{i}][canonical_text]", row["canonical_text"] %></label>
      <label>Type <%= select_tag "claims[#{i}][claim_type]", options_for_select(Claim::TYPES, row["claim_type"]) %></label>
      <details<%= " open" if row["topics"].any? %>><summary>Topics (optional)</summary><%= render "shared/topic_picker", name: "claims[#{i}][topics][]", selected: row["topics"] %></details>
      <label><%= check_box_tag "claims[#{i}][affirms_not_private_individual]", "1", row["affirms"] %> I affirm this claim is not about an identifiable private individual.</label>
      <% row["warnings"].each do |w| %><span class="warning"><%= w[:detail] || w["detail"] %></span><% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <%= f.submit "Check wording", name: "check", class: "secondary" %>
  <%= f.submit "Record claims" %>
<% end %>
